### Local demo credentials are for development only.
### IntelliJ IDEA HTTP Client supports Basic authorization syntax.
### Run using --spring.profiles.active=local

### Activate a crisis alert
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/crisis-alerts
Authorization: Basic caregiver-alert-001 demo123
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "childId": "child-001",
  "description": "El niño necesita apoyo durante un cambio de rutina"
}

### List alerts (authorized caregiver)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/crisis-alerts?childId=child-001
Authorization: Basic caregiver-alert-002 demo123

### My queued in-app notices
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/crisis-alerts/notifications
Authorization: Basic caregiver-alert-002 demo123

### Mark attended (replace UUID with the created ID)
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/v1/crisis-alerts/REPLACE_WITH_ALERT_UUID/attend
Authorization: Basic caregiver-alert-002 demo123

### Close alert (replace UUID with the created ID)
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/v1/crisis-alerts/REPLACE_WITH_ALERT_UUID/close
Authorization: Basic caregiver-alert-001 demo123
